@startuml 11-seq-negotiation
!include _style.iuml
title xtxp.link content negotiation

participant "Client" as c
participant "xtxp.link\ngateway" as gw
participant "Directory" as dir
participant "Hosting node" as node

c -> gw : GET https://xtxp.link/{host}/{path}@{ref}
gw -> dir : who hosts {host}/{path}?
dir --> gw : hosting node + the branch\nor vector named by {ref}

alt Accept: application/xtxp+xml
  gw -> node : open patch stream
  gw --> c : raw XTXP patch stream
else Accept: text/html
  gw --> c : rendered current state as HTML\n+ forms that POST edits\n+ link "open in native client" → xtxp://{host}/{path}@{ref}
end

note over gw
  A server cannot tell whether an xtxp:// handler
  is installed, and a meta refresh to a missing
  handler fails silently, so the hand-off is a link.
end note

note over c, node
  {ref} is @live (an ordinary website as it is now), @main,
  a branch name, or a state vector. The last @ always starts the ref;
  a bare URL redirects to the default ref.
end note
@enduml
